#====================================================================
# DRAFT - GCC Ada build-only GNAT seed under the HarmonyOS XPM policy
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-gcc-ada-ohos-xpm-seed-loader
trigger_tool:           gcc|gnat|gnatmake|gnat1|musl|mmap|conan|binary-sign-tool
phase:                  bootstrap|compilation|runtime|testing
error_signature:        PermissionError: \[Errno 13\] Permission denied.*mmap|
                         MAP_XPM.*EACCES|
                         PROT_EXEC.*EACCES|
                         Error loading shared library lib(isl|mpc|mpfr|gmp|z)\.so|
                         /proc/self/fd/9|
                         SHORT_NEEDED_DIAGNOSTIC

severity:               3
category:               harmonyos|gcc|ada|gnat|bootstrap|musl|xpm|signing
match_keywords:         GCC Ada, GNAT seed, Alpine musl, MAP_XPM, XPM,
                         binary-sign-tool, PT_INTERP, /proc/self/fd/9,
                         short NEEDED, owner identity, signed loader
title:                  Run XPM dependency checks inside the signed GNAT seed loader, not a Python preloader

root_cause: >
  GCC's Ada frontend is written in Ada, so a native GCC Ada build needs an
  existing GNAT seed. A checksum-pinned Alpine AArch64/musl seed has compatible
  code generation, but HarmonyOS XPM rejects its unsigned executable mappings
  and shared dependencies. Signing the copied ELF files is necessary but not
  sufficient when a Python launcher first performs MAP_XPM or PROT_EXEC mmap:
  that mmap runs under the Python process signing identity, not the signed seed
  process identity, and returns EACCES even from writable cache and HAP files
  directories. The patched musl loader already performs check_xpm while loading
  each dependency. Once the signed seed is exec'ed with PT_INTERP set to
  /proc/self/fd/9, those checks run in the correct seed execution context.

affected_scope: >
  Native HarmonyOS builds of GCC Ada or other bootstrapped language frontends
  that use a checksum-pinned AArch64/musl compiler seed with shared dependencies.

verification_cmd: >
  CI_PACKAGES="archives/g/gcc-ada/9.5.0" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh;
  require seed_probe.o, SHORT_NEEDED_DIAGNOSTIC=pass, and clean CI #31486.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           signed-seed-fd-loader-xpm-context
rec_description: >
  Treat the seed as a build-only verified source input. Copy it to an executable
  application files location; replace long dependency NEEDED names with short
  names; build a package-owned musl loader that uses MAP_XPM for file-backed
  segments; rewrite seed PT_INTERP to /proc/self/fd/9; sign the copied seed,
  short-name libraries and loader. The launcher must only open the loader,
  preserve it on fd 9, set the seed library path, and exec the signed seed.
  Leave XPM dependency checks to the loader after exec. Discard the seed from
  the final package.
rec_command: >
  loader_fd=open(signed_loader); dup2(loader_fd, 9); set_inheritable(9, true);
  execv(signed_seed, argv); patched musl loader performs check_xpm(fd) while
  resolving the signed short-name dependencies.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-build-only-bootstrap-loader

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      native-signed-launcher
fallback_description: >
  If the platform Python cannot preserve the loader descriptor through exec,
  use a small signed native launcher with the same fd 9 and exec contract. Do
  not move dependency mapping back into the launcher process.
fallback_command:       signed-launcher <signed-seed> <args>
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          native-exec-wrapper

forbid_1_pattern:       mmap\(.*MAP_XPM|mmap\(.*PROT_EXEC
forbid_1_reason:        A Python-side pre-map uses the launcher signing identity and duplicates the loader's own XPM check.
forbid_1_consequence:   Clean workers fail with EACCES before the signed seed or musl loader executes.

forbid_2_pattern:       package.*(Alpine|seed|libisl|libmpc|libmpfr|libgmp)
forbid_2_reason:        The Alpine GNAT closure is licensed and verified as a build-only bootstrap input, not a runtime package component.
forbid_2_consequence:   The final Conan package leaks an undeclared foreign runtime and loses relocatability.

principles:             P013, P016
similar_to:             E260, DRAFT-patchelf-breaks-ohos-signing
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-gcc-ada-ohos-xpm-seed-loader.md
last_updated:           2026-08-26
source_event:           archives/g/gcc-ada/9.5.0 issue #2281

authors:                wxjshr
source_pr:              OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper/build_in_harmonyos!6116
source_commit:          2da8d6c87193635bb5fdaa3927ec18f918fad815

metrics_success_count:  2
metrics_fail_count:     4
metrics_confidence:     1.0
